# Normalize to LF in the repository; Git still checks out native line endings on Windows.
# Keeps `cargo fmt --check` and diffs consistent wherever this is built.
* text=auto

*.rs    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# **Shell scripts must keep LF wherever they are checked out**, and this one is load-bearing rather
# than cosmetic. `sh` on Linux and macOS treats a trailing CR as part of the interpreter path, so a
# CRLF checkout of `tools/dist/cmd.sh` fails with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" —
# a message that names the right path and gives no hint why.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Note the lock file is deliberately *not* listed as binary: it is a text file, it wants normalizing
# like everything else, and it is committed because these are binaries and a tool with a floating
# dependency tree is one that stops working quietly.
